-- statement:
--   WordSpace(n,d) is the complex vector space of functions from words Fin n → Fin d (length-n words over d letters) to ℂ, and wordRep(n,d) is the representation of the symmetric group on n letters in which a permutation g sends a function f to the function a ↦ f(a∘g), that is, it acts by permuting word positions. For a representation ρ and vector v, cyclic(ρ,v) is the subrepresentation spanned over ℂ by all translates ρ(g)v. For a Young diagram μ, a Tableau is a bijection from Fin n onto the cells of μ, and canonicalTableau picks one such bijection when μ has n cells. For a tableau t, rowWord(t) is the word recording the row coordinate of the cell assigned to each position, taking values in Fin(μ.colLen 0), and columnGroup(t) is the subgroup of permutations that preserve the column coordinate of every position. The polytabloid of t is the sum over g in the column group of sign(g) times wordRep applied to g and the indicator function of the word rowWord(t). The Specht module of t is the cyclic subrepresentation of wordRep(n, μ.colLen 0) generated by this polytabloid, with spechtRep its induced symmetric-group representation. Finally kronecker(a,b,t) is the complex dimension of the space of intertwining maps from the Specht representation of t to the tensor product of the Specht representations of a and b, for tableaux a, b, t of shapes α, β, μ on n points. The block also opens an empty UniversalTensorSquares namespace and states no theorem.
